 "existing_tips": [
  "'Succedeva spesso' (It happened often) – repeated occurrence of events = imperfetto, not passato pro",
  "Passato prossimo is the most-used past tense in spoken Italian – used for completed events, like Eng",
  "Imperfect subjunctive after past tense main clause.",
  "'A' contracts with articles: al (a+il), alla (a+la), ai (a+i), alle (a+le). Mandatory with definite ",
  "'Noi' imperative form used for suggestions.",
  "Vorrei che + imperfect subjunctive for wishes.",
  "Reflexive verbs use \"essere\" in compound tenses, and the participle agrees: \"Mi sono alzata\" (f).",
  "Italian uses imperfetto more broadly than English uses 'was doing' – includes 'used to' and 'would ("
 ]
